          <div class="figure-caption">
            <strong>Fig. 1.</strong> End-to-end four-tier architecture of the proposed PRevent framework, illustrating the interaction between Tier 1 (React 18 presentation views), Tier 2 (Express/Node.js ingestion, hunk line-mapping, and structural feature extraction), Tier 3 (four-module hybrid security engine), and Tier 4 (GitHub REST API v3, Google OSV API, and MongoDB Atlas persistence).
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <p>
        As illustrated in <strong>Fig. 1</strong>, the four operational tiers collaborate through well-defined asynchronous interfaces. In <strong>Tier 1 (React 18 Presentation Tier)</strong>, maintainers interact with four dedicated modules: (i) the <em>Security Overview Dashboard &amp; Live GitHub Open PR Browser</em>, which fetches open Pull Requests from any public or private GitHub repository; (ii) the <em>PR Analysis &amp; Interactive Issue Resolution Workbench</em>, which renders line-level findings and one-click patch controls; (iii) the <em>Dependency Intelligence Inspector</em>, which breaks down package-level decision factors and precautions; and (iv) the <em>AI Engine &amp; 22-Scenario Verification Suite</em>. In <strong>Tier 2 (Express Ingestion Tier)</strong>, <code>githubClient.js</code> retrieves PR metadata and unified diffs from <code>api.github.com</code> using Bearer token authentication with an automatic unauthenticated fallback if a fine-grained token lacks repository scope. Next, <code>diffParser.js</code> reconstructs exact added/removed line numbers, and <code>featureExtractor.js</code> builds an 8-dimensional structural indicator vector. These representations feed <strong>Tier 3 (Hybrid Security Engine)</strong>, where Modules 1, 2, and 3 execute concurrently and converge in Module 4 (<code>riskEngine.js</code>), which synchronizes scan reports and resolution audit trails with <strong>Tier 4 (Cloud &amp; Persistence Tier)</strong> via Google OSV and MongoDB Atlas.
      </p>

      <h3 class="subsection-heading">B. Stage 1 &amp; Stage 2: Unified Diff Parsing and Context-Sensitive Co-Occurrence Rule Engine</h3>
      <p>
        Let an incoming Pull Request comprise a set of modified files <em>F</em> = {<em>f</em><sub>1</sub>, <em>f</em><sub>2</sub>, &hellip;, <em>f<sub>m</sub></em>}. For each file <em>f<sub>i</sub></em> &isin; <em>F</em>, the Unified Diff Parser (<code>diffParser.js</code>) parses the unified git patch by tracking hunk range headers of the form <code>@@ -a,b +c,d @@</code>. It assigns an exact destination line number <em>l</em> &isin; &#8469; to every added line (<em>L<sub>i</sub></em><sup>+</sup>) and removed line (<em>L<sub>i</sub></em><sup>&minus;</sup>) while stripping diff metadata markers (<code>+++</code>, <code>---</code>). Each file <em>f<sub>i</sub></em> is mapped to a canonical file category:
      </p>
      <div class="equation">
        <span>&tau;(<em>f<sub>i</sub></em>) &isin; {workflow, dependency_manifest, python_setup, javascript, python, shell, other}</span>
        <span>(1)</span>
      </div>
      <p>
        Next, the Structural Feature Extractor (<code>featureExtractor.js</code>) computes an 8-dimensional behavioral indicator vector <strong>x</strong><sub>struct</sub>(<em>F</em>) across all added lines <em>L</em><sup>+</sup> = &cup;<sub><em>i</em>=1</sub><sup><em>m</em></sup> <em>L<sub>i</sub></em><sup>+</sup>, capturing: (1) <code>dependency_change</code> &isin; {0,1}, (2) <code>dangerous_api_count</code>, (3) <code>network_activity_count</code>, (4) <code>secret_access_count</code>, (5) <code>obfuscation_indicators</code>, (6) <code>workflow_permission_change</code> &isin; {0,1}, (7) <code>total_added_lines</code>, and (8) <code>changed_file_types</code>.
      </p>
      <p>
        To eliminate false alarms on benign application code that reads environment variables for local port configuration or invokes standard REST APIs, Module 1 (<code>ruleEngine.js</code>) enforces context-sensitive co-occurrence rules. <strong>Fig. 2</strong> depicts the hunk coordinate extraction and four-branch rule evaluation logic of Stages 1 and 2.
      </p>

      <!-- FULL WIDTH FIGURE 2 (STATIC CO-OCCURRENCE & DIFF HUNK FLOW) -->
      <div class="full-width-block">
        <div class="figure-box">
          <svg viewBox="0 0 820 235" width="100%" height="auto" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" style="font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;">
            <!-- Left Input: Diff Hunk -->
            <rect x="12" y="38" width="168" height="155" rx="6" fill="#f8fafc" stroke="#334155" stroke-width="1.5"/>
            <text x="96" y="56" font-size="9.5" font-weight="bold" text-anchor="middle" fill="#0f172a">Stage 1: Hunk Parser</text>
            <text x="96" y="69" font-size="8" text-anchor="middle" fill="#475569">(diffParser.js)</text>
            <rect x="22" y="78" width="148" height="48" rx="4" fill="#ffffff" stroke="#64748b"/>
            <text x="96" y="94" font-size="8" font-family="monospace" text-anchor="middle" fill="#0f172a">@@ -14,3 +14,8 @@</text>
            <text x="96" y="107" font-size="8" text-anchor="middle" fill="#15803d">+ Added Lines L_i^+ (Line l)</text>
            <text x="96" y="119" font-size="8" text-anchor="middle" fill="#b91c1c">- Removed Lines L_i^-</text>
            <rect x="22" y="134" width="148" height="48" rx="4" fill="#ffffff" stroke="#64748b"/>
            <text x="96" y="149" font-size="8.5" font-weight="bold" text-anchor="middle" fill="#0f172a">File Classifier &tau;(f_i)</text>
            <text x="96" y="162" font-size="7.5" text-anchor="middle">Python / JS / Manifest /</text>
            <text x="96" y="173" font-size="7.5" text-anchor="middle">Setup.py / GitHub Workflow</text>

            <!-- Center: Co-Occurrence & Multi-Branch Gate -->
            <rect x="208" y="12" width="385" height="210" rx="6" fill="#eef2ff" stroke="#3730a3" stroke-width="1.5"/>
            <text x="400" y="29" font-size="9.5" font-weight="bold" text-anchor="middle" fill="#1e1b4b">Stage 2: Context-Sensitive Static Rule Engine (ruleEngine.js)</text>

            <!-- Branch 1: Co-Occurrence Gate -->
            <rect x="220" y="38" width="360" height="48" rx="4" fill="#ffffff" stroke="#4338ca"/>
            <text x="400" y="53" font-size="8.5" font-weight="bold" text-anchor="middle" fill="#1e1b4b">Branch 1: Intra-Diff Credential-to-Network Co-Occurrence Gate</text>
            <text x="400" y="66" font-size="8" text-anchor="middle">Source S_sec(f_i) [os.environ, process.env, .ssh/id_rsa, .npmrc] &and; Sink S_net(f_i) [POST, fetch, curl]</text>
            <text x="400" y="79" font-size="7.5" font-style="italic" text-anchor="middle" fill="#15803d">If S_sec=1 &and; S_net=0 &rarr; Suppressed as Benign Config (0% FPR) | If &Phi;_exfil = 1 &rarr; SEC-EXFIL-001..003</text>

            <!-- Branch 2: Obfuscation -->
            <rect x="220" y="94" width="360" height="38" rx="4" fill="#ffffff" stroke="#4338ca"/>
            <text x="400" y="109" font-size="8.5" font-weight="bold" text-anchor="middle" fill="#1e1b4b">Branch 2: Multi-Layer Obfuscation &amp; Dynamic Execution Gate</text>
            <text x="400" y="122" font-size="8" text-anchor="middle">exec(base64.b64decode) | Buffer+eval/Function | marshal(zlib) | powershell -enc | \x.. hex &rarr; OBF-EXEC-001..005</text>

            <!-- Branch 3: Install Hooks -->
            <rect x="220" y="140" width="360" height="36" rx="4" fill="#ffffff" stroke="#4338ca"/>
            <text x="400" y="154" font-size="8.5" font-weight="bold" text-anchor="middle" fill="#1e1b4b">Branch 3: Package Lifecycle Hook Gate (package.json &amp; setup.py)</text>
            <text x="400" y="167" font-size="8" text-anchor="middle">preinstall / postinstall (curl | sh, wget, node -e) &amp; setup.py (/dev/tcp/ reverse shell) &rarr; DEP-SCRIPT-001..002</text>

            <!-- Branch 4: CI Workflow -->
            <rect x="220" y="182" width="360" height="34" rx="4" fill="#ffffff" stroke="#4338ca"/>
            <text x="400" y="196" font-size="8.5" font-weight="bold" text-anchor="middle" fill="#1e1b4b">Branch 4: CI/CD Workflow Privilege Escalation Gate (.github/workflows/*.yml)</text>
            <text x="400" y="209" font-size="8" text-anchor="middle">pull_request_target + permissions: write-all + ${{ toJSON(secrets) }} curl dump &rarr; CI-WORKFLOW-001..002</text>

            <!-- Right Output: Structured Finding & Patch -->
            <rect x="620" y="38" width="188" height="155" rx="6" fill="#fff1f2" stroke="#be123c" stroke-width="1.5"/>
            <text x="714" y="56" font-size="9.5" font-weight="bold" text-anchor="middle" fill="#881337">Structured Rule Output</text>
            <rect x="632" y="68" width="164" height="112" rx="4" fill="#ffffff" stroke="#e11d48"/>
            <text x="714" y="84" font-size="8" font-weight="bold" text-anchor="middle" fill="#881337">Finding Telemetry Object</text>
            <text x="714" y="99" font-size="8" text-anchor="middle">&bull; Rule ID &amp; Threat Category</text>
            <text x="714" y="113" font-size="8" text-anchor="middle">&bull; Exact File &amp; Line Number (l)</text>
            <text x="714" y="127" font-size="8" text-anchor="middle">&bull; Offending Code Snippet</text>
            <text x="714" y="141" font-size="8" text-anchor="middle">&bull; Plain-English Explanation</text>
            <text x="714" y="155" font-size="8" font-weight="bold" text-anchor="middle" fill="#15803d">&bull; Copy-Ready Remediation</text>
            <text x="714" y="167" font-size="8" font-weight="bold" text-anchor="middle" fill="#15803d">Patch (suggested_patch)</text>

            <!-- Connectors -->
            <line x1="180" y1="115" x2="208" y2="115" stroke="#334155" stroke-width="1.5"/>
            <line x1="593" y1="62" x2="620" y2="95" stroke="#be123c" stroke-width="1.2"/>
            <line x1="593" y1="113" x2="620" y2="110" stroke="#be123c" stroke-width="1.2"/>
            <line x1="593" y1="158" x2="620" y2="125" stroke="#be123c" stroke-width="1.2"/>
            <line x1="593" y1="199" x2="620" y2="140" stroke="#be123c" stroke-width="1.2"/>
          </svg>
          <div class="figure-caption">
            <strong>Fig. 2.</strong> Stage 1 and Stage 2 execution flow: Unified git diff hunk coordinate mapping (<code>diffParser.js</code>) feeding the four-branch context-sensitive static rule engine (<code>ruleEngine.js</code>). Isolated credential reads (<em>S</em><sub>sec</sub> = 1, <em>S</em><sub>net</sub> = 0) are filtered out to prevent false positives, whereas co-occurring source-to-sink exfiltration (&Phi;<sub>exfil</sub> = 1), multi-stage obfuscation, lifecycle hooks, and CI workflow poisoning emit line-accurate findings and remediation patches.
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <p>
        Referring to <strong>Fig. 2</strong>, the four deterministic evaluation branches in Module 1 operate as follows:
      </p>
      <ol>
        <li><strong>Co-Occurring Credential Exfiltration (<code>SEC-EXFIL-001</code> to <code>003</code>):</strong> Let <em>S</em><sub>sec</sub>(<em>f<sub>i</sub></em>) &isin; {0,1} denote whether added lines in <em>f<sub>i</sub></em> access environment secrets (<code>os.environ</code>, <code>process.env</code>, <code>SECRET</code>, <code>TOKEN</code>), and let <em>S</em><sub>net</sub>(<em>f<sub>i</sub></em>) &isin; {0,1} denote whether <em>f<sub>i</sub></em> invokes an outbound network transfer or webhook sink. As shown in Branch 1 of <strong>Fig. 2</strong>, if <em>S</em><sub>sec</sub>(<em>f<sub>i</sub></em>) = 1 but <em>S</em><sub>net</sub>(<em>f<sub>i</sub></em>) = 0, the engine classifies the hunk as a benign configuration read. Rule <code>SEC-EXFIL-001</code> triggers if and only if both conditions co-occur within the diff:
          <div class="equation">
            <span>&Phi;<sub>exfil</sub>(<em>f<sub>i</sub></em>) = <em>S</em><sub>sec</sub>(<em>f<sub>i</sub></em>) &and; <em>S</em><sub>net</sub>(<em>f<sub>i</sub></em>) = 1</span>
            <span>(2)</span>
          </div>
          Rules <code>SEC-EXFIL-002</code> and <code>SEC-EXFIL-003</code> further detect direct file reads of SSH private keys (<code>~/.ssh/id_rsa</code>, <code>.aws/credentials</code>) and npm authentication tokens (<code>.npmrc</code> <code>_authToken</code>).
        </li>
        <li><strong>Multi-Layer Obfuscation &amp; Dynamic Execution (<code>OBF-EXEC-001</code> to <code>005</code>):</strong> As shown in Branch 2 of <strong>Fig. 2</strong>, detects Base64 decode-and-execute chains in Python (<code>exec(base64.b64decode(...))</code>) and JavaScript (<code>Buffer.from(..., 'base64')</code> with <code>eval</code> or <code>new Function</code>), compressed bytecode loading via <code>marshal.loads(zlib.decompress(...))</code>, hidden Windows PowerShell encoded commands (<code>powershell -NoP -W Hidden -enc</code>), and high-density hex escape sequences (<code>\x..</code>).</li>
        <li><strong>Malicious Build Lifecycle Hooks (<code>DEP-SCRIPT-001</code>, <code>002</code>):</strong> Branch 3 of <strong>Fig. 2</strong> flags <code>package.json</code> <code>preinstall</code>/<code>postinstall</code> hooks invoking <code>curl | sh</code>, <code>wget</code>, or <code>node -e</code>, as well as Python <code>setup.py</code> scripts opening <code>/dev/tcp/</code> reverse shells.</li>
        <li><strong>CI/CD Workflow Poisoning (<code>CI-WORKFLOW-001</code>, <code>002</code>):</strong> Branch 4 of <strong>Fig. 2</strong> audits <code>.github/workflows/*.yml</code> for <code>pull_request_target</code> combined with <code>permissions: write-all</code> and outbound transmission of <code>${{ toJSON(secrets) }}</code>.</li>
      </ol>

      <h3 class="subsection-heading">C. Stage 3: Five-Stage Multi-Ecosystem Dependency Intelligence Engine</h3>
      <p>
        Module 2 (<code>dependencyScanner.js</code>) inspects dependency additions and version transitions across six ecosystems: <code>npm</code> (<code>package.json</code>), <code>PyPI</code> (<code>requirements.txt</code>, <code>pyproject.toml</code>, <code>setup.py</code>), <code>Maven</code> (<code>pom.xml</code>, <code>build.gradle</code>), <code>Go</code> (<code>go.mod</code>), <code>Cargo</code> (<code>Cargo.toml</code>), and <code>Container/CI</code> (<code>Dockerfile</code>). <strong>Fig. 3</strong> illustrates the five-stage dependency intelligence pipeline and the bounded Levenshtein edit-distance verification mechanism.
      </p>

      <!-- FULL WIDTH FIGURE 3 (5-STAGE DEPENDENCY INTELLIGENCE PIPELINE) -->
      <div class="full-width-block">
        <div class="figure-box">
          <svg viewBox="0 0 820 195" width="100%" height="auto" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" style="font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;">
            <!-- Stage 1 -->
            <rect x="10" y="20" width="146" height="150" rx="5" fill="#f8fafc" stroke="#334155" stroke-width="1.4"/>
            <text x="83" y="38" font-size="9" font-weight="bold" text-anchor="middle" fill="#0f172a">Stage 1: 6-Ecosystem</text>
            <text x="83" y="50" font-size="9" font-weight="bold" text-anchor="middle" fill="#0f172a">Manifest Parser</text>
            <line x1="20" y1="57" x2="146" y2="57" stroke="#cbd5e1"/>
            <text x="83" y="72" font-size="8" text-anchor="middle">&bull; npm (package.json)</text>
            <text x="83" y="86" font-size="8" text-anchor="middle">&bull; PyPI (requirements.txt)</text>
            <text x="83" y="100" font-size="8" text-anchor="middle">&bull; Maven (pom.xml)</text>
            <text x="83" y="114" font-size="8" text-anchor="middle">&bull; Go (go.mod)</text>
            <text x="83" y="128" font-size="8" text-anchor="middle">&bull; Cargo (Cargo.toml)</text>
            <text x="83" y="142" font-size="8" text-anchor="middle">&bull; Docker (Dockerfile)</text>

            <!-- Stage 2 -->
            <rect x="174" y="20" width="146" height="150" rx="5" fill="#f8fafc" stroke="#334155" stroke-width="1.4"/>
            <text x="247" y="38" font-size="9" font-weight="bold" text-anchor="middle" fill="#0f172a">Stage 2: Version Delta</text>
            <text x="247" y="50" font-size="9" font-weight="bold" text-anchor="middle" fill="#0f172a">Reconstruction</text>
            <line x1="184" y1="57" x2="310" y2="57" stroke="#cbd5e1"/>
            <text x="247" y="76" font-size="8" text-anchor="middle">1. Parse Removed Lines L^-</text>
            <text x="247" y="88" font-size="8" text-anchor="middle">to record baseline v_old</text>
            <text x="247" y="106" font-size="8" text-anchor="middle">2. Parse Added Lines L^+</text>
            <text x="247" y="118" font-size="8" text-anchor="middle">to extract target v_new</text>
            <text x="247" y="138" font-size="8" font-weight="bold" text-anchor="middle" fill="#3730a3">Classify Transition:</text>
            <text x="247" y="151" font-size="8" text-anchor="middle">ADDED vs. UPDATED</text>

            <!-- Stage 3 -->
            <rect x="338" y="20" width="146" height="150" rx="5" fill="#fff1f2" stroke="#be123c" stroke-width="1.4"/>
            <text x="411" y="38" font-size="9" font-weight="bold" text-anchor="middle" fill="#881337">Stage 3: OpenSSF &amp;</text>
            <text x="411" y="50" font-size="9" font-weight="bold" text-anchor="middle" fill="#881337">Malicious Registry</text>
            <line x1="348" y1="57" x2="474" y2="57" stroke="#fecdd3"/>
            <text x="411" y="73" font-size="8" text-anchor="middle">Matches known hijacked</text>
            <text x="411" y="85" font-size="8" text-anchor="middle">&amp; protestware releases:</text>
            <text x="411" y="102" font-size="7.8" font-family="monospace" text-anchor="middle">event-stream@3.3.6</text>
            <text x="411" y="115" font-size="7.8" font-family="monospace" text-anchor="middle">ua-parser-js@0.7.29</text>
            <text x="411" y="128" font-size="7.8" font-family="monospace" text-anchor="middle">node-ipc@10.1.1</text>
            <text x="411" y="141" font-size="7.8" font-family="monospace" text-anchor="middle">colors@1.4.44-liberty-2</text>
            <text x="411" y="156" font-size="8" font-weight="bold" text-anchor="middle" fill="#be123c">CRITICAL (+40 pts)</text>

            <!-- Stage 4 -->
            <rect x="502" y="20" width="146" height="150" rx="5" fill="#eef2ff" stroke="#3730a3" stroke-width="1.4"/>
            <text x="575" y="38" font-size="9" font-weight="bold" text-anchor="middle" fill="#1e1b4b">Stage 4: Bounded</text>
            <text x="575" y="50" font-size="9" font-weight="bold" text-anchor="middle" fill="#1e1b4b">Levenshtein (d_L = 1)</text>
            <line x1="512" y1="57" x2="638" y2="57" stroke="#c7d2fe"/>
            <text x="575" y="73" font-size="8" text-anchor="middle">DP Edit Distance against</text>
            <text x="575" y="85" font-size="8" text-anchor="middle">popular registry targets T_e:</text>
            <text x="575" y="102" font-size="7.8" font-family="monospace" text-anchor="middle">reqeusts &rarr; requests</text>
            <text x="575" y="115" font-size="7.8" font-family="monospace" text-anchor="middle">colourama &rarr; colorama</text>
            <text x="575" y="128" font-size="7.8" font-family="monospace" text-anchor="middle">axois &rarr; axios</text>
            <text x="575" y="141" font-size="7.8" font-family="monospace" text-anchor="middle">lodahs &rarr; lodash</text>
            <text x="575" y="156" font-size="8" font-weight="bold" text-anchor="middle" fill="#3730a3">Auto-Synthesizes Fix t*</text>

            <!-- Stage 5 -->
            <rect x="666" y="20" width="144" height="150" rx="5" fill="#f0fdf4" stroke="#15803d" stroke-width="1.4"/>
            <text x="738" y="38" font-size="9" font-weight="bold" text-anchor="middle" fill="#064e3b">Stage 5: Live OSV API</text>
            <text x="738" y="50" font-size="9" font-weight="bold" text-anchor="middle" fill="#064e3b">&amp; Maintainer Guidance</text>
            <line x1="676" y1="57" x2="800" y2="57" stroke="#bbf7d0"/>
            <text x="738" y="73" font-size="8" text-anchor="middle">POST api.osv.dev/v1/query</text>
            <text x="738" y="86" font-size="8" text-anchor="middle">+ Offline CVE Database</text>
            <text x="738" y="104" font-size="8" font-weight="bold" text-anchor="middle" fill="#064e3b">Enriches Every Package:</text>
            <text x="738" y="118" font-size="8" text-anchor="middle">1. Decision Factors</text>
            <text x="738" y="132" font-size="8" text-anchor="middle">2. Security Precautions</text>
            <text x="738" y="146" font-size="8" text-anchor="middle">3. Safe Version Pin Patch</text>

            <!-- Arrows -->
            <line x1="156" y1="95" x2="174" y2="95" stroke="#334155" stroke-width="1.5"/>
            <line x1="320" y1="95" x2="338" y2="95" stroke="#334155" stroke-width="1.5"/>
            <line x1="484" y1="95" x2="502" y2="95" stroke="#334155" stroke-width="1.5"/>
            <line x1="648" y1="95" x2="666" y2="95" stroke="#334155" stroke-width="1.5"/>
          </svg>
          <div class="figure-caption">
            <strong>Fig. 3.</strong> Five-stage multi-ecosystem supply-chain dependency intelligence pipeline (<code>dependencyScanner.js</code>), showing manifest parsing across six ecosystems (Stage 1), version transition reconstruction (Stage 2), OpenSSF/Datadog malicious release matching (Stage 3), bounded Levenshtein edit-distance (<em>d<sub>L</sub></em> = 1) typosquatting detection (Stage 4), and live Google OSV API lookup with maintainer Decision Factor enrichment (Stage 5).
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <p>
        As depicted in <strong>Fig. 3</strong>, each dependency extracted in Stage 1 undergoes version delta reconstruction in Stage 2 by matching removed manifest lines (<em>v</em><sub>old</sub>) against added manifest lines (<em>v</em><sub>new</sub>). In Stage 3, the package is screened against OpenSSF and Datadog malicious package signatures. To detect previously unseen typosquatting attacks in Stage 4 of <strong>Fig. 3</strong>, PRevent evaluates the Levenshtein edit distance <em>d<sub>L</sub></em>(<em>p</em>, <em>t</em>) between each newly introduced package name <em>p</em> and a curated set of high-download ecosystem targets <em>T<sub>e</sub></em> (e.g., <code>requests</code>, <code>colorama</code>, <code>urllib3</code>, <code>lodash</code>, <code>express</code>, <code>axios</code>, <code>chalk</code>). For strings <em>a</em> and <em>b</em>, the dynamic programming matrix <em>D</em>(<em>i</em>, <em>j</em>) is computed as:
      </p>
      <div class="equation">
        <span><em>D</em>(<em>i</em>, <em>j</em>) = min { <em>D</em>(<em>i</em>&minus;1, <em>j</em>) + 1, &nbsp;<em>D</em>(<em>i</em>, <em>j</em>&minus;1) + 1, &nbsp;<em>D</em>(<em>i</em>&minus;1, <em>j</em>&minus;1) + &#120128;(<em>a<sub>i</sub></em> &ne; <em>b<sub>j</sub></em>) }</span>
        <span>(3)</span>
      </div>
      <p>
        Any package <em>p</em> &notin; <em>T<sub>e</sub></em> with |<em>p</em>| &ge; 5 satisfying <em>d<sub>L</sub></em>(<em>p</em>, <em>t</em><sup>*</sup>) = 1 for some <em>t</em><sup>*</sup> &isin; <em>T<sub>e</sub></em> is immediately flagged under rule <code>TYPOSQUAT-LEVENSHTEIN-RULE</code> (CRITICAL, +40 points), and an automated patch replacing <em>p</em> with <em>t</em><sup>*</sup> is synthesized. Finally, in Stage 5 of <strong>Fig. 3</strong>, each package version is queried against the Google OSV API (<code>POST https://api.osv.dev/v1/query</code>), attaching structured <em>Decision Factors</em>, <em>Security Precautions</em>, and <em>Resolution Steps</em> to every dependency record.
      </p>

      <h3 class="subsection-heading">D. Stage 4: In-Memory TF-IDF + L2 Logistic Regression Classifier</h3>
      <p>
        Module 3 (<code>mlDetector.js</code>) provides an explainable statistical machine learning layer that operates entirely in memory without external CSV files. <strong>Fig. 4</strong> illustrates the end-to-end feature extraction, sublinear TF-IDF vectorization, L2 normalization, and calibrated Logistic Regression inference architecture of Module 3.
      </p>

      <!-- FULL WIDTH FIGURE 4 (TF-IDF + L2 LOGISTIC REGRESSION PIPELINE) -->
      <div class="full-width-block">
        <div class="figure-box">
          <svg viewBox="0 0 820 185" width="100%" height="auto" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" style="font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;">
            <!-- Box 1: Input & Tokenizer -->
            <rect x="10" y="18" width="152" height="148" rx="5" fill="#f8fafc" stroke="#334155" stroke-width="1.4"/>
            <text x="86" y="36" font-size="9" font-weight="bold" text-anchor="middle" fill="#0f172a">1. Lexical N-Gram</text>
            <text x="86" y="48" font-size="9" font-weight="bold" text-anchor="middle" fill="#0f172a">Tokenizer</text>
            <line x1="20" y1="55" x2="152" y2="55" stroke="#cbd5e1"/>
            <text x="86" y="72" font-size="8" text-anchor="middle">&bull; Alphanumeric &amp; API</text>
            <text x="86" y="84" font-size="8" text-anchor="middle">Unigrams (w_k)</text>
            <text x="86" y="102" font-size="8" text-anchor="middle">&bull; Contiguous Bigrams</text>
            <text x="86" y="114" font-size="8" text-anchor="middle">(w_k, w_{k+1})</text>
            <text x="86" y="132" font-size="8" text-anchor="middle">&bull; File-Type Prefixes</text>
            <text x="86" y="145" font-size="7.5" font-family="monospace" text-anchor="middle">__filetype_&lt;type&gt;__</text>

            <!-- Box 2: Structural Token Augmentation -->
            <rect x="178" y="18" width="164" height="148" rx="5" fill="#eef2ff" stroke="#3730a3" stroke-width="1.4"/>
            <text x="260" y="36" font-size="9" font-weight="bold" text-anchor="middle" fill="#1e1b4b">2. Domain Security</text>
            <text x="260" y="48" font-size="9" font-weight="bold" text-anchor="middle" fill="#1e1b4b">Token Injection</text>
            <line x1="188" y1="55" x2="332" y2="55" stroke="#c7d2fe"/>
            <text x="260" y="72" font-size="7.5" font-family="monospace" text-anchor="middle" fill="#312e81">__feat_secret_access__</text>
            <text x="260" y="88" font-size="7.5" font-family="monospace" text-anchor="middle" fill="#312e81">__feat_network_exfil__</text>
            <text x="260" y="104" font-size="7.5" font-family="monospace" text-anchor="middle" fill="#312e81">__feat_ci_or_install_hook__</text>
            <text x="260" y="120" font-size="7.5" font-family="monospace" text-anchor="middle" fill="#312e81">__feat_obfuscation_exec__</text>
            <text x="260" y="136" font-size="7.5" font-family="monospace" text-anchor="middle" fill="#312e81">__feat_malicious_pkg__</text>
            <text x="260" y="153" font-size="7.8" font-style="italic" text-anchor="middle">High-Signal Composite Anchors</text>

            <!-- Box 3: Sublinear TF-IDF & L2 Normalization -->
            <rect x="358" y="18" width="154" height="148" rx="5" fill="#f8fafc" stroke="#334155" stroke-width="1.4"/>
            <text x="435" y="36" font-size="9" font-weight="bold" text-anchor="middle" fill="#0f172a">3. Sublinear TF-IDF</text>
            <text x="435" y="48" font-size="9" font-weight="bold" text-anchor="middle" fill="#0f172a">&amp; L2 Normalization</text>
            <line x1="368" y1="55" x2="502" y2="55" stroke="#cbd5e1"/>
            <text x="435" y="73" font-size="8" text-anchor="middle">Active Vocab |V| = 814</text>
            <text x="435" y="89" font-size="8" text-anchor="middle">tf = 1 + ln(count(t, d))</text>
            <text x="435" y="105" font-size="8" text-anchor="middle">idf = ln((N+1)/(df+1)) + 1</text>
            <text x="435" y="125" font-size="8" font-weight="bold" text-anchor="middle" fill="#0f172a">Unit Vector Projection:</text>
            <text x="435" y="140" font-size="8" text-anchor="middle">v_hat = v / (||v||_2 + &epsilon;)</text>

            <!-- Box 4: L2 Logistic Regression -->
            <rect x="528" y="18" width="136" height="148" rx="5" fill="#eef2ff" stroke="#3730a3" stroke-width="1.4"/>
            <text x="596" y="36" font-size="9" font-weight="bold" text-anchor="middle" fill="#1e1b4b">4. L2-Regularized</text>
            <text x="596" y="48" font-size="9" font-weight="bold" text-anchor="middle" fill="#1e1b4b">Logistic Regression</text>
            <line x1="538" y1="55" x2="654" y2="55" stroke="#c7d2fe"/>
            <text x="596" y="74" font-size="8" text-anchor="middle">Trained on N = 36</text>
            <text x="596" y="86" font-size="8" text-anchor="middle">Balanced Diff Patterns</text>
            <text x="596" y="106" font-size="8" font-weight="bold" text-anchor="middle" fill="#1e1b4b">Linear Logit &amp; Sigmoid:</text>
            <text x="596" y="121" font-size="8" text-anchor="middle">z = w^T v_hat + b</text>
            <text x="596" y="136" font-size="8" text-anchor="middle">&sigma;(z) = 1 / (1 + e^{-z})</text>
            <text x="596" y="152" font-size="7.5" text-anchor="middle">Latency: 0.31 ms</text>

            <!-- Box 5: Calibrated Output & Explainability -->
            <rect x="680" y="18" width="130" height="148" rx="5" fill="#f0fdf4" stroke="#15803d" stroke-width="1.4"/>
            <text x="745" y="36" font-size="9" font-weight="bold" text-anchor="middle" fill="#064e3b">5. Explainable AI</text>
            <text x="745" y="48" font-size="9" font-weight="bold" text-anchor="middle" fill="#064e3b">Risk Attribution</text>
            <line x1="690" y1="55" x2="800" y2="55" stroke="#bbf7d0"/>
            <text x="745" y="73" font-size="8" text-anchor="middle">Calibrated Probability</text>
            <text x="745" y="86" font-size="8" font-weight="bold" text-anchor="middle" fill="#064e3b">P_ML &isin; [0.00, 1.00]</text>
            <text x="745" y="104" font-size="8" text-anchor="middle">Bounded Risk Bonus:</text>
            <text x="745" y="117" font-size="8" font-weight="bold" text-anchor="middle" fill="#15803d">S_ML = round(15 &middot; P_ML)</text>
            <text x="745" y="135" font-size="8" text-anchor="middle">Ranks Top Positive</text>
            <text x="745" y="148" font-size="8" text-anchor="middle">Tokens (w_j &middot; v_hat_j)</text>

            <!-- Connectors -->
            <line x1="162" y1="92" x2="178" y2="92" stroke="#334155" stroke-width="1.5"/>
            <line x1="342" y1="92" x2="358" y2="92" stroke="#334155" stroke-width="1.5"/>
            <line x1="512" y1="92" x2="528" y2="92" stroke="#334155" stroke-width="1.5"/>
            <line x1="664" y1="92" x2="680" y2="92" stroke="#334155" stroke-width="1.5"/>
          </svg>
          <div class="figure-caption">
            <strong>Fig. 4.</strong> In-memory TF-IDF + L2-regularized Logistic Regression pipeline (<code>mlDetector.js</code>), illustrating (1) lexical unigram/bigram extraction, (2) injection of five domain-specific structural security tokens, (3) 814-dimensional sublinear TF-IDF vectorization and unit-norm projection, (4) L2-penalized sigmoid inference, and (5) bounded risk contribution (0–15 points) with per-token weight attribution.
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <p>
        As shown in <strong>Fig. 4</strong>, given a unified diff text <em>d</em>, Step 1 extracts word unigrams, word bigrams, and file-type indicators, while Step 2 injects five composite structural security tokens (<code>__feat_secret_access__</code>, <code>__feat_network_exfil__</code>, <code>__feat_ci_or_install_hook__</code>, <code>__feat_obfuscation_exec__</code>, and <code>__feat_malicious_pkg__</code>). In Step 3 of <strong>Fig. 4</strong>, sublinear Term Frequency and smoothed Inverse Document Frequency across the training corpus of size <em>N</em> = 36 (|<em>V</em>| = 814 active features) are calculated as:
      </p>
      <div class="equation">
        <span>tf(<em>t</em>, <em>d</em>) = 1 + ln(count(<em>t</em>, <em>d</em>)), &nbsp;&nbsp; idf(<em>t</em>) = ln((<em>N</em> + 1) / (df(<em>t</em>) + 1)) + 1</span>
        <span>(4)</span>
      </div>
      <p>
        In Step 4 of <strong>Fig. 4</strong>, the L2-normalized TF-IDF feature vector <strong>v&#770;</strong>(<em>d</em>) is scored by an L2-regularized Logistic Regression classifier trained via batch gradient descent on the penalized cross-entropy objective:
      </p>
      <div class="equation">
        <span><em>L</em>(<strong>w</strong>, <em>b</em>) = &minus;(1/<em>N</em>) &sum; [ <em>y<sub>i</sub></em> ln &sigma;(<em>z<sub>i</sub></em>) + (1 &minus; <em>y<sub>i</sub></em>) ln(1 &minus; &sigma;(<em>z<sub>i</sub></em>)) ] + (&lambda;/2) ||<strong>w</strong>||<sub>2</sub><sup>2</sup></span>
        <span>(5)</span>
      </div>
      <p>
        where <em>z<sub>i</sub></em> = <strong>w</strong><sup>T</sup><strong>v&#770;</strong><sub><em>i</em></sub> + <em>b</em> and &sigma;(<em>z</em>) = (1 + <em>e</em><sup>&minus;<em>z</em></sup>)<sup>&minus;1</sup>. Finally, in Step 5 of <strong>Fig. 4</strong>, when the calibrated suspicion probability <em>P</em><sub>ML</sub> &ge; 0.55, the classifier flags the PR, surfaces the top positive feature weights <em>w<sub>j</sub>v&#770;<sub>j</sub></em> for human verification, and contributes <em>S</em><sub>ML</sub> = round(15 &middot; <em>P</em><sub>ML</sub>) &isin; [0, 15] points to the overall risk assessment.
      </p>

      <h3 class="subsection-heading">E. Stage 5: Deduplicated Risk Aggregation &amp; Closed-Loop Interactive Remediation</h3>
      <p>
        Module 4 (<code>riskEngine.js</code>) synthesizes all open (unresolved) findings <em>F</em><sub>open</sub> and the AI suspicion score into a composite risk score <em>R</em> &isin; [0, 100]. To prevent repeated triggers of the same rule within a single file from skewing the score, category-level deduplication is enforced over unique active categories <em>C</em><sub>open</sub>:
      </p>
      <div class="equation">
        <span><em>R</em>(<em>F</em><sub>open</sub>, <em>P</em><sub>ML</sub>) = min( 100, &nbsp;&sum;<sub><em>c</em> &isin; <em>C</em><sub>open</sub></sub> <em>W</em>(<em>c</em>) + &#120128;(<em>F</em><sub>open</sub> &ne; &empty; &or; <em>P</em><sub>ML</sub> &ge; 0.55) &middot; <em>S</em><sub>ML</sub> )</span>
        <span>(6)</span>
      </div>
      <p>
        where category weights are calibrated as: Malicious Dependency (+40), Secret Exfiltration (+35), Vulnerable Dependency (+30), Dangerous Install Script (+30), Obfuscated Execution (+25), and CI Workflow Tampering (+20). <strong>Fig. 5</strong> illustrates the closed-loop interactive remediation sequence and state transition when a maintainer resolves findings in the PRevent Workbench.
      </p>

      <!-- FULL WIDTH FIGURE 5 (CLOSED-LOOP REMEDIATION SEQUENCE DIAGRAM) -->
      <div class="full-width-block">
        <div class="figure-box">
          <svg viewBox="0 0 820 225" width="100%" height="auto" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" style="font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;">
            <!-- Participant Headers -->
            <rect x="20" y="12" width="120" height="32" rx="4" fill="#0f172a" stroke="#0f172a"/>
            <text x="80" y="32" font-size="9" font-weight="bold" text-anchor="middle" fill="#ffffff">Maintainer</text>

            <rect x="195" y="12" width="145" height="32" rx="4" fill="#eef2ff" stroke="#3730a3" stroke-width="1.4"/>
            <text x="267" y="27" font-size="8.5" font-weight="bold" text-anchor="middle" fill="#1e1b4b">React PR Workbench</text>
            <text x="267" y="38" font-size="7.5" text-anchor="middle" fill="#3730a3">(PRAnalysisPage.tsx)</text>

            <rect x="395" y="12" width="145" height="32" rx="4" fill="#f8fafc" stroke="#334155" stroke-width="1.4"/>
            <text x="467" y="27" font-size="8.5" font-weight="bold" text-anchor="middle" fill="#0f172a">Express REST API</text>
            <text x="467" y="38" font-size="7.5" text-anchor="middle" fill="#475569">(/api/scans/:id/resolve)</text>

            <rect x="590" y="12" width="110" height="32" rx="4" fill="#fff1f2" stroke="#be123c" stroke-width="1.4"/>
            <text x="645" y="27" font-size="8.5" font-weight="bold" text-anchor="middle" fill="#881337">Risk Engine</text>
            <text x="645" y="38" font-size="7.5" text-anchor="middle" fill="#be123c">(riskEngine.js)</text>

            <rect x="720" y="12" width="88" height="32" rx="4" fill="#f0fdf4" stroke="#15803d" stroke-width="1.4"/>
            <text x="764" y="27" font-size="8.5" font-weight="bold" text-anchor="middle" fill="#064e3b">MongoDB</text>
            <text x="764" y="38" font-size="7.5" text-anchor="middle" fill="#15803d">(ScanReport)</text>

            <!-- Lifelines -->
            <line x1="80" y1="44" x2="80" y2="212" stroke="#94a3b8" stroke-dasharray="3,3"/>
            <line x1="267" y1="44" x2="267" y2="212" stroke="#94a3b8" stroke-dasharray="3,3"/>
            <line x1="467" y1="44" x2="467" y2="212" stroke="#94a3b8" stroke-dasharray="3,3"/>
            <line x1="645" y1="44" x2="645" y2="212" stroke="#94a3b8" stroke-dasharray="3,3"/>
            <line x1="764" y1="44" x2="764" y2="212" stroke="#94a3b8" stroke-dasharray="3,3"/>

            <!-- Step 1 -->
            <line x1="80" y1="62" x2="267" y2="62" stroke="#0f172a" stroke-width="1.3"/>
            <text x="173" y="57" font-size="8" font-weight="bold" text-anchor="middle">1. Clicks "Copy Patch" &amp; "Resolve Issue" (f_k)</text>

            <!-- Step 2 -->
            <line x1="267" y1="84" x2="467" y2="84" stroke="#3730a3" stroke-width="1.3"/>
            <text x="367" y="79" font-size="8" text-anchor="middle">2. POST /api/scans/:id/resolve {finding_id, note}</text>

            <!-- Step 3 -->
            <line x1="467" y1="106" x2="764" y2="106" stroke="#15803d" stroke-width="1.3"/>
            <text x="615" y="101" font-size="8" text-anchor="middle">3. Load ScanReport &amp; resolved_finding_ids</text>

            <!-- Step 4 -->
            <line x1="467" y1="132" x2="645" y2="132" stroke="#be123c" stroke-width="1.3"/>
            <text x="556" y="127" font-size="8" font-weight="bold" text-anchor="middle">4. Re-evaluate Eq. (6) on F_open = F \ (resolved &cup; {f_k})</text>

            <!-- Step 5 -->
            <line x1="645" y1="154" x2="467" y2="154" stroke="#be123c" stroke-width="1.3" stroke-dasharray="4,2"/>
            <text x="556" y="149" font-size="8" text-anchor="middle">5. Return Recalculated Score R' (e.g., 85 &rarr; 0 LOW)</text>

            <!-- Step 6 -->
            <line x1="467" y1="176" x2="764" y2="176" stroke="#15803d" stroke-width="1.3"/>
            <text x="615" y="171" font-size="8" text-anchor="middle">6. Upsert ScanReport + Append resolution_log Audit</text>

            <!-- Step 7 -->
            <line x1="467" y1="198" x2="80" y2="198" stroke="#0f172a" stroke-width="1.4"/>
            <text x="273" y="193" font-size="8" font-weight="bold" text-anchor="middle" fill="#15803d">7. Animate Risk Drop (CRITICAL 85 &rarr; LOW 0) &amp; Mark REMEDIATED_AND_VERIFIED</text>
          </svg>
          <div class="figure-caption">
            <strong>Fig. 5.</strong> Closed-loop interactive remediation sequence diagram. Resolving a finding <em>f<sub>k</sub></em> dynamically removes it from the open finding set <em>F</em><sub>open</sub>, recalculates the deduplicated composite risk score <em>R'</em> via Eq. (6), logs a timestamped audit entry in MongoDB Atlas, and transitions the Pull Request to <code>REMEDIATED_AND_VERIFIED</code>.
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <p>
        Walking through <strong>Fig. 5</strong>, when a maintainer inspects a flagged code line or dependency, copies the synthesized remediation patch, and clicks <strong>Resolve Issue</strong> on finding <em>f<sub>k</sub></em> (Step 1), the React workbench dispatches a <code>POST /api/scans/:id/resolve</code> request to the Express backend (Step 2). The server retrieves the current <code>ScanReport</code> from MongoDB Atlas (Step 3) and invokes <code>riskEngine.js</code> (Step 4), which appends <em>f<sub>k</sub></em> to <code>resolved_finding_ids</code> and recomputes Eq. (6) over the remaining unresolved categories <em>C</em><sub>open</sub> (Step 5). Once all deterministic findings are resolved (<em>F</em><sub>open</sub> = &empty;), the AI suspicion bonus <em>S</em><sub>ML</sub> is suppressed so that the Pull Request score drops cleanly to <em>R'</em> = 0 (<code>LOW</code>). The updated report and immutable <code>resolution_log</code> entry are saved to MongoDB Atlas (Step 6), and the UI gauge animates the transition to <code>REMEDIATED_AND_VERIFIED</code> (Step 7).
      </p>

      <!-- SECTION IV -->
      <h2 class="section-heading">IV. Experimental Setup &amp; Results Analysis</h2>

      <h3 class="subsection-heading">A. Implementation Setup and Verification Protocol</h3>
      <p>
        PRevent was implemented on Node.js v22.20.0, Express.js v4.19, Mongoose v8.5 (connected to MongoDB Atlas database <code>PR_issue_resolver</code>), and React 18.3 with TypeScript 5.5 and Tailwind CSS 3.4. We evaluated the system across a 22-scenario multi-vector benchmark catalog (<code>TC-001</code> to <code>TC-022</code>) plus 3 system-level verification tests (25 automated tests in <code>backend/tests/scanner.test.js</code>) as well as live public GitHub Pull Requests from repositories including <code>expressjs/express</code> and <code>axios/axios</code>.
      </p>

