      <!-- SECTION V -->
      <h2 class="section-heading">V. Conclusion and Future Work</h2>
      <p>
        This paper presented <strong>PRevent</strong>, a full-stack MERN decision-support security framework that detects and remediates malicious Pull Requests and risky supply-chain dependency updates prior to merge. By uniting intra-diff source-to-sink static rules (Fig. 2), six-ecosystem manifest analysis and Levenshtein edit-distance typosquatting detection with live Google OSV advisories (Fig. 3), and an explainable in-memory TF-IDF + L2 Logistic Regression classifier (Fig. 4), PRevent achieves 100% detection recall with zero false positives across our 22-scenario benchmark suite (Figs. 6 and 7). Furthermore, its closed-loop remediation workbench (Fig. 5) empowers maintainers with clear decision factors, security precautions, copy-ready patches, and dynamic risk score recalculation. Future work will extend PRevent with cross-file Tree-sitter call-graph taint analysis, automated GitHub App commit suggestion bots, and temporal contributor provenance modeling.
      </p>

